{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Maintainer-directed Phase 4 scope expansion (2026-09-01): the Janitor Cleanup epic must remove every genuinely scheduled deprecation and every retired compatibility shim proven no longer reachable. Current scheduled removals are transition(force_close=...), transition(force=True), and explicit hosted-OpenAI openai-chat: selection; custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints retain Chat Completions because that is a live transport constraint, not the deprecated hosted fallback. For retired shims, ticket acceptance criteria must require both a semantic/static production-reference census and a string/dynamic-import/getattr/monkeypatch census. Tests that only exercise a retired shim do not establish a production consumer; update or delete them with the shim. Persistent-event readers, stored-data migrations, and other on-disk compatibility remain separate migration concerns. Consumer-facing aliases marked permanent or explicitly retained are inventoried for individual maintainer decisions and are not blanket-approved by this rule. The full inventory and boundary are recorded in .joe-janitor/report-2026-08-29.md."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788286324983342001,"uuid":"82d87045-ebcc-48d4-bc15-3f0d736258ba"}